WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.750
It's Thursday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Here's what shipped at Microsoft in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.420
Start building. This year's free Hour of AI activities are out,

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.820
for grades 3 to 12.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.140
For teachers, a free 30-minute Microsoft Elevate course gets you ready.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.580
In class, Minecraft Education's free new lesson,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.290
Field Agent, shows how data steers an AI agent.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.260
Students help a farm agent build better barns,

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.010
fence different animals and harvest crops at peak ripeness.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.650
A door too small for a cow?

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.320
Minecraft Education calls that a debugging opportunity.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.180
No AI runs while they play, and there's a free demo, plus teacher guides.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.330
For school IT, Baseline security mode 2026 is rolling out: 24 new settings.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.990
Guests need MFA, outsiders wait in the Teams lobby,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:13.450
and simulation mode tests it first.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.490
Coding students? VS Code agents can now reply with a chart or mockup,

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:20.730
if you turn it on.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.030
And for campus builders,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.190
the Foundry Dev Pack installs Microsoft's agent tools in one go.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.130
Want to practise?

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.590
AI Skills Navigator now has free hands-on labs, no licence needed.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.050
And soon,

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:42.650
Learning Agent will send staff tips in Teams to build their Copilot skills.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.920
The fine print?

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:51.940
Two hijacked releases of Microsoft's agent-framework Python package carried a credential stealer.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.550
Installed either? Roll back to 1.26.0, and change every key it could reach.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.110
After hours, Minecraft's upcoming winter drop is The Deep Freeze,

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:08.460
with ice caves and ice that cracks.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.130
Watch out for the frostbite, a frozen zombie whose ice balls slow you down.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.400
Then build with new snow and packed ice bricks, and a full calcite set.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.310
A farm, an app or a snow castle: whatever it is, start building.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.690
On the release board: shipped, and still shipping.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.410
That was 24 hours at Microsoft. Tomorrow, there's more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.
